WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.908 --> 00:00:14.909
and Perda scurried out of the tree trunk.

2
00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:19.791
The forest was dark and spooky, and Zann didn't want to go any deeper into it.

3
00:00:20.511 --> 00:00:23.492
Besides, he didn't want to get too far from the wormhole.

4
00:00:23.512 --> 00:00:25.593
"Look, a cave!"

5
00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:26.513
Perda pointed.

6
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:28.054
"Let's hide in there."

7
00:00:28.854 --> 00:00:33.793
At the cave's entrance, Zann used the small amount of energy he had left to do a quick

8
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.734
Life Force Locator spell.

9
00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:39.697
The cave was empty, so he and Perda huddled inside.

10
00:00:40.358 --> 00:00:46.363
As the two monsters continued to fight outside, Zann and Perda caught their breath and talked about what

11
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:46.843
had happened.

12
00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:51.167
"Did you see whether Darb, Gliss, and Zing stayed together?"

13
00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:52.087
Zann asked.

14
00:00:52.107 --> 00:00:53.569
"I couldn't tell."

15
00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:54.810
Perda looked worried.

16
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:59.193
"If Darb gets separated from Gliss "I know.

17
00:00:59.654 --> 00:01:02.396
Without magic, he'd be helpless in the vortex."

18
00:01:03.604 --> 00:01:05.746
Zann's mind flashed again to Venna.

19
00:01:06.547 --> 00:01:07.487
What had become of her?

20
00:01:07.928 --> 00:01:08.848
And what about Morb?

21
00:01:09.589 --> 00:01:13.032
Without his stolen magic, he was a Void, just like Darb.

22
00:01:13.912 --> 00:01:16.695
"We need to figure out how to find them," Perda said.

23
00:01:16.715 --> 00:01:19.057
"Fast!" "How?"

24
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:21.138
Zann glanced out of the cave.

25
00:01:21.158 --> 00:01:26.683
"Even if we can make it past those two monsters and back to the wormhole, we can't even

26
00:01:26.743 --> 00:01:28.544
navigate our way through the vortex.

27
00:01:29.265 --> 00:01:30.826
Let alone find our friends."

28
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.028
He looked at Perda.

29
00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:36.693
"I can't believe I dragged you all into this," he mumbled.

30
00:01:37.554 --> 00:01:38.214
Perda shrugged.

31
00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:41.295
"You didn't drag me—I wanted to come."

32
00:01:42.236 --> 00:01:43.476
Zann gave a small chuckle.

33
00:01:43.977 --> 00:01:46.898
"Well, we've both said we want to be explorers.

34
00:01:47.938 --> 00:01:50.299
Now here we are—exploring."

35
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.601
Perda peered out from the cave and then smiled.

36
00:01:53.621 --> 00:01:56.242
"Look! They're running off!"

37
00:01:57.762 --> 00:01:58.503
Zann looked out.

38
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:03.745
The battling monsters had stopped fighting and were now racing away in opposite directions.

39
00:02:04.705 --> 00:02:06.125
"That's weird," he said.

40
00:02:06.145 --> 00:02:08.006
"I wonder why they're leaving."

41
00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:09.546
"Who cares?"

42
00:02:09.946 --> 00:02:10.487
said Perda.

43
00:02:10.987 --> 00:02:13.147
"This could be our chance to get back to the wormhole."

44
00:02:14.068 --> 00:02:15.188
She crawled out of the cave.

45
00:02:15.208 --> 00:02:16.668
"Come on!"

46
00:02:17.829 --> 00:02:22.810
They raced out of the forest and across the dark plain, dodging random bursts of energy.

47
00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.051
Zann could see the wormhole winking at them just ahead.

48
00:02:26.891 --> 00:02:28.892
Being in the vortex was pretty scary.

49
00:02:29.624 --> 00:02:32.885
But they'd just discovered that certain worlds were even scarier.

50
00:02:32.905 --> 00:02:35.226
"Hurry!" he called to Perda.

51
00:02:35.246 --> 00:02:37.066
"We have to—argh!"

52
00:02:38.187 --> 00:02:43.968
Zann suddenly felt a stinging sensation, as if he were being stuck with burning needles all over his

53
00:02:44.028 --> 00:02:47.829
body. He fell to the ground, twitching and groaning.

54
00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:49.750
"What's happening?"

55
00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.590
Perda cried in a shaky voice.

56
00:02:52.391 --> 00:02:56.392
Out of the corner of his eye, Zann saw her fall, twitching, beside him.

57
00:02:57.312 --> 00:02:59.453
Then a new creature stepped into view.

58
00:03:00.193 --> 00:03:06.036
It was much smaller than the dragon or the deca-stinger— in fact, it wasn't much bigger than Zing.

59
00:03:07.156 --> 00:03:08.717
It didn't look very scary either.

60
00:03:09.177 --> 00:03:11.858
It resembled a hairy walking mop.

61
00:03:12.798 --> 00:03:15.019
Even so, Zann shivered when he saw it.

62
00:03:15.039 --> 00:03:17.160
"Oh no," he said.

63
00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.081
"It's a scatter beast!"

64
00:03:20.462 --> 00:03:22.102
"That's a scatter beast?"

65
00:03:22.382 --> 00:03:22.883
Perda said.

66
00:03:22.903 --> 00:03:25.824
"The thing that knocked your parents off course?"

67
00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:27.941
Zann couldn't answer.

68
00:03:28.361 --> 00:03:32.524
As the scatter beast crept closer, the stinging sensations grew worse.

69
00:03:33.284 --> 00:03:37.227
Besides, Zann didn't know much more about scatter beasts than Perda did.

70
00:03:38.308 --> 00:03:42.891
All he knew was that they threw off chaotic energy that confused the magic of others.

71
00:03:44.152 --> 00:03:47.314
He struggled to regain control of his body, but it was no use.

72
00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.016
The scatter beast was still approaching.

73
00:03:50.716 --> 00:03:56.300
A skinny tentacle appeared from amid the dirty, grayish hair and stretched toward the kids.

74
00:03:57.392 --> 00:04:02.213
Zann could only stare at it, mesmerized by the spiral-shaped claw at the end.

75
00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:04.574
"We have to get away!"

76
00:04:04.734 --> 00:04:05.314
Perda cried.

77
00:04:06.095 --> 00:04:07.235
She rubbed her hands together.

78
00:04:07.255 --> 00:04:11.996
"Blast!" A small sizzle of energy spit out of her hand.

79
00:04:12.837 --> 00:04:17.198
It made it halfway to the scatter beast before suddenly doubling back toward the kids.

80
00:04:17.998 --> 00:04:20.839
At the same time, it swelled into a fireball.

81
00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.379
"Look out!"

82
00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:24.480
Zann yelled, throwing himself aside.

83
00:04:25.284 --> 00:04:26.925
Perda rolled away just in time too.

84
00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:31.588
The fireball blasted a large hole in the rocky ground between them.

85
00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:35.291
Zann tried to turn to make sure Perda was okay.

86
00:04:35.691 --> 00:04:36.812
But he couldn't move anymore.

87
00:04:37.693 --> 00:04:40.555
He realized he'd thrown himself even closer to the scatter beast.

88
00:04:41.315 --> 00:04:47.860
All Zann could do now was stare helplessly as the creature moved toward him, its claw aimed at

89
00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:48.480
his forehead.

90
00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.222
Zann knew he should be scared.

91
00:04:51.782 --> 00:04:53.744
After all, he was about to die.

92
00:04:54.784 --> 00:04:57.685
But instead the only thing he felt was regret.

93
00:04:58.546 --> 00:05:03.528
He regretted that he would never find his parents, that Boz would never know what had happened to

94
00:05:03.588 --> 00:05:08.650
him, and that he'd never have the chance to make up with Gliss— or even find out if

95
00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:14.973
she and the others had survived Then, out of the corner of his eye, he noticed something strange.

96
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:22.216
A sparkling rain of colorful glitter was falling gently from the sky, seemingly out of nowhere.

97
00:05:23.336 --> 00:05:28.979
At first Zann assumed it was an illusion, that the scatter beast's energy was affecting his vision.

98
00:05:29.859 --> 00:05:33.620
Then the first bits of glitter touched the scatter beast.

99
00:05:34.201 --> 00:05:39.923
They sizzled and burned some of its fur, causing the beast to jump back and howl with pain.

100
00:05:40.704 --> 00:05:46.806
Its wild energy went even wilder, sparking fires here and there and making the ground shudder.

101
00:05:46.826 --> 00:05:50.848
"Huh?" Zann mumbled through numb lips.

102
00:05:51.724 --> 00:05:56.769
Then he felt someone grab him by the arm and drag him across the hard, rocky ground.

103
00:05:57.589 --> 00:06:02.694
A moment later he felt the increasingly familiar sensation of passing through a wormhole.

104
00:06:03.555 --> 00:06:06.397
The vortex felt almost welcoming after Fardark.

105
00:06:07.158 --> 00:06:10.541
When he felt Perda bump against him, Zann was relieved.

106
00:06:11.061 --> 00:06:12.242
They'd both made it out.

107
00:06:12.863 --> 00:06:13.904
But who had rescued them?

108
00:06:13.924 --> 00:06:18.428
"That was close," an irritated voice snapped.

109
00:06:19.248 --> 00:06:22.774
"I thought I warned you about the wormholes, boy."

110
00:06:23.536 --> 00:06:26.480
Zann blinked, his vision swimming back into focus.

111
00:06:27.242 --> 00:06:31.469
He gasped as he finally got a good look at the person who had grabbed him.

112
00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:32.490
It was
